# FABLE-SONNET-CALLABLE-PRIORITY-20260923-130 (closes plan :181/:182/:212/
# :214-priority/:216). Universal priority by resolved binding: a callable
# head is ALWAYS a call, in every surface form -- colon, paren, vertical --
# never assignment or declaration, and not a special case per form. `foo`
# is callable and takes one argument; each call form must run foo's own
# body, observed in what foo prints: `foo 1 5`, `foo 1 6`, `foo 1 7` --
# not silently nothing, not some other operation.  hits and last are foo's
# hidden inputs (Q52, the author 2026-09-28): each call starts from the
# unit's 0 and its bare writes change only that activation's values, so
# hits prints 1 every time (the unit's field cached in foo and published
# back would print 1, 2, 3).
int: hits 0
int: last 0

fn: foo (int: n) int
    hits: hits + 1
    last: n
    c.printf: "foo %d %d\n" hits last
    return: 0
end: foo

foo: 5
foo(6)
foo:
    7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
